<title>RUSSIA: Russia training Indian pilots on fighter jets.</title>
<headline>Russia training Indian pilots on fighter jets.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia has begun training 55 Indian military pilots to fly Su-30MK fighters that will be delivered to New Delhi's air force later this year, a Russian air force spokesman said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;These pilots will have a three-month course on the Su-30MK's operation, including test flights at the base at Zukovsky, near Moscow,&quot; the spokesman said.</p>
<p>He said Russia would supply the first eight Su-30MK aircraft to India this March. Russia and India last year signed a $1.8 billion contract for 40 such planes by the year 2000.</p>
</text>
